11
00:02:30.698 --> 00:02:34.368
<i>Guns are hot. Target qualifies.
Engage at your discretion.</i>

12
00:02:34.452 --> 00:02:35.619
Roger that.

13
00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:44.920
Civilian bus, one klick south.

14
00:02:47.465 --> 00:02:50.384
<i>Too close, Major.
Get the strike on this pass, or abort.</i>

15
00:02:51.886 --> 00:02:52.970
Copy that.

16
00:02:53.971 --> 00:02:54.972
I can get it.

17
00:02:55.097 --> 00:02:56.098
<i>Rifle when ready.</i>

18
00:02:56.182 --> 00:02:57.683
Master arm hot.

19
00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:59.310
Fly the laser.

20
00:02:59.393 --> 00:03:00.728
<i>Target, lasered.</i>

21
00:03:01.604 --> 00:03:03.355
Three, two,

22
00:03:04.273 --> 00:03:06.484
one, rifle.

23
00:03:06.942 --> 00:03:10.279
Missile away.
Time of flight, 10 seconds.

24
00:03:20.456 --> 00:03:21.499
Splash.

25
00:03:37.181 --> 00:03:38.516
Good kill.

26
00:03:41.185 --> 00:03:43.103
Well, they don't call it
a Hellfire for nothing.

27
00:03:43.187 --> 00:03:46.232
Best use of $68,000 taxpayer dollars
I've seen today.

28
00:03:46.315 --> 00:03:48.609
Master arm off. Weapon's safe.

29
00:03:49.318 --> 00:03:50.694
Laser safe.

30
00:03:51.529 --> 00:03:52.655
Damage assessment.

31
00:03:56.075 --> 00:03:57.701
Come on, Carlos. Tighten up.

32
00:04:00.538 --> 00:04:01.539
What's the body count?

33
00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.837
I count six, sir.

34
00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.714
But good luck figuring out
which bits go in what casket.

35
00:04:11.841 --> 00:04:14.134
Setting a course for J-bad.

36
00:04:16.095 --> 00:04:17.388
Watch yourself, Tommy.

37
00:04:17.555 --> 00:04:19.598
You're beak-to-beak
with that Reaper relieving you.

38
00:04:19.682 --> 00:04:21.016
- Yes, sir.
- Two o'clock.

39
00:04:21.475 --> 00:04:24.687
MQ-9. American engineering
at its finest.

40
00:04:25.896 --> 00:04:28.816
All right. Hand off to
Captain Christie for recovery.

41
00:05:42.848 --> 00:05:44.058
Is that real?

42
00:05:46.143 --> 00:05:49.229
You ever get to, like,
fly in a war or something?

43
00:05:51.357 --> 00:05:54.360
Blew away six Taliban
in Pakistan just today.

44
00:05:55.653 --> 00:05:56.987
Now I'm going home to barbeque.

45
00:05:57.363 --> 00:05:58.697
Yeah, right.

46
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.735
- It's not my fault.
- Travis, get back here right now.

47
00:06:37.736 --> 00:06:40.239
Get back here
and pick up the crap you just dumped!

48
00:06:40.322 --> 00:06:42.783
Do not walk away from me, young man!

49
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.910
Do not walk away from me.

50
00:06:46.203 --> 00:06:47.538
Travis!

51
00:06:50.499 --> 00:06:52.543
Feel free to step in anytime, Tommy.

52
00:06:52.626 --> 00:06:53.836
I'll talk to him.

53
00:06:54.545 --> 00:06:58.298
I got a call from the principal's office.
He was fighting with another boy.

54
00:06:58.382 --> 00:06:59.758
Did he Win?

55
00:07:01.677 --> 00:07:04.680
Hey, Jesse, how's that book?
You recommend it?

56
00:07:05.556 --> 00:07:08.684
- Sorry the house looks like...
- A bomb hit it?

57
00:07:10.019 --> 00:07:11.228
I didn't say it.

58
00:07:11.645 --> 00:07:14.440
I'd ask how your day was,
but there's a limit...

59
00:07:14.523 --> 00:07:15.649
- I know. I'm sorry.
- How many times

60
00:07:15.733 --> 00:07:18.068
- I can ask the same question.
- Thank you for not asking.

61
00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:22.031
You know he's flunking math.
He needs a tutor.

62
00:07:22.906 --> 00:07:26.201
How much will that cost?
Can't you help him?

63
00:07:27.327 --> 00:07:30.164
Where do you think he gets it from?
I'm the reason he's flunking.

64
00:07:30.247 --> 00:07:31.707
That's true.

65
00:07:32.332 --> 00:07:34.001
I start nights tomorrow.

66
00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.671
Okay.

67
00:08:13.957 --> 00:08:15.751
You look miles away.

68
00:08:19.797 --> 00:08:20.964
Seven thousand?

69
00:08:23.592 --> 00:08:24.885
That's a joke.

70
00:08:29.306 --> 00:08:31.308
I think I'm gonna go get a glass of water.

71
00:08:32.851 --> 00:08:34.478
You need anything?

72
00:08:37.648 --> 00:08:38.816
Yeah, I do.

73
00:08:54.081 --> 00:08:55.499
Living the dream, Tommy.

74
00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.043
Hey, Dan.

75
00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.572
Ladies and gentlemen,
the aircraft you're looking at

76
00:09:26.655 --> 00:09:28.824
is not the future of war.

77
00:09:28.907 --> 00:09:30.993
It is the here and fucking now.

78
00:09:31.577 --> 00:09:32.995
Any time of day or night,

79
00:09:33.078 --> 00:09:36.165
there are dozens of
these things in the sky

80
00:09:36.248 --> 00:09:37.624
above our theaters of operation.

81
00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:41.587
And most are currently working in the
Garden of Eden they call Afghanistan.

82
00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.070
Where they're starting to think
it's their new national bird.

83
00:09:45.174 --> 00:09:46.466
Now, I assume you know

84
00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.802
we don't fly them all the way there
from here in Vegas,

85
00:09:48.886 --> 00:09:50.637
but I guess I shouldn't assume anything.

86
00:09:50.721 --> 00:09:53.056
I got food in my fridge
older than most of you.

87
00:09:53.182 --> 00:09:55.976
Now, all take-offs and landings occur

88
00:09:56.059 --> 00:09:58.729
in and around
whatever godforsaken place

89
00:09:58.812 --> 00:10:00.731
we're at war with that day.

90
00:10:00.814 --> 00:10:03.984
That's 'cause these things are a bitch
to take off and land.

91
00:10:04.067 --> 00:10:06.320
So once they're airborne,
that's when we take over.

92
00:10:06.403 --> 00:10:08.864
And these gentlemen here are gonna
take you through the nuts and bolts

93
00:10:08.947 --> 00:10:10.282
of exactly how we do that.

94
00:10:11.408 --> 00:10:15.037
But before they do, there's one thing
I want to say about this program.

95
00:10:15.495 --> 00:10:17.748
We get a lot of shit from the public.

96
00:10:18.207 --> 00:10:21.001
And I've heard
all the bleeding heart arguments.

97
00:10:21.084 --> 00:10:23.295
I've read all the fucking bumper stickers.

98
00:10:23.378 --> 00:10:25.047
"It's not the air force,
it's the chair-force,"

99
00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.465
"waging a Wii war."

100
00:10:27.007 --> 00:10:29.927
It's all a waste of breath
because the United States Air Force

101
00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.429
is ordering more drones than jets.

102
00:10:32.971 --> 00:10:36.391
Excuse me, "remotely piloted aircraft."
You can call them whatever you want.

103
00:10:37.559 --> 00:10:39.436
Drones aren't going anywhere.

104
00:10:40.103 --> 00:10:41.980
In fact, they're going everywhere.

105
00:10:46.109 --> 00:10:48.779
But don't think I believe
my own shit either.

106
00:10:48.946 --> 00:10:52.449
'Cause we like to dress it up
in fancy language.

107
00:10:53.951 --> 00:10:57.788
Prosecuting a target, a surgical strike,

108
00:10:57.871 --> 00:10:59.706
neutralizing the threat.

109
00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.459
Make no fucking mistake about it.

110
00:11:03.961 --> 00:11:05.462
We are killing people.

111
00:11:06.255 --> 00:11:08.590
So I'm gonna drill this into your heads
every goddamn day.

112
00:11:08.674 --> 00:11:10.634
This ain't fucking PlayStation.

113
00:11:12.636 --> 00:11:16.390
Even though the brass
don't like to admit it,

114
00:11:16.473 --> 00:11:18.475
our operation was modeled on Xbox.

115
00:11:19.726 --> 00:11:21.520
And half of you were recruited in malls

116
00:11:21.603 --> 00:11:24.564
precisely because
you are a bunch of fucking gamers.

117
00:11:24.648 --> 00:11:27.150
And war is now a first-person shooter.

118
00:11:27.234 --> 00:11:29.319
But you pull a trigger here,

119
00:11:29.403 --> 00:11:30.904
it's for fucking real.

120
00:11:33.991 --> 00:11:36.493
Ain't a bunch of pixels
you're blowing up.

121
00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:43.834
It's flesh and fucking blood.

122
00:11:46.044 --> 00:11:48.547
You pull a trigger here,
someone's gonna go away.

123
00:11:49.673 --> 00:11:52.009
Now, go away.

124
00:11:54.136 --> 00:11:55.595
Dismissed.

125
00:11:55.679 --> 00:11:57.139
Atten-hut!

126
00:11:57.889 --> 00:12:00.517
That's a lot of recruits
for a war that's ending.

127
00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:03.270
So what'd you log?
3,000 hours in F-16s,

128
00:12:03.353 --> 00:12:06.356
six tours, 200 combat sorties
before you got here?

129
00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:09.860
Now they give them 40 hours in
a fucking Cessna and send them to me.

130
00:12:09.943 --> 00:12:11.695
And pretty soon they won't even do that.

131
00:12:11.778 --> 00:12:14.823
Just shove a joystick
in their clammy mitts on day one.

132
00:12:16.325 --> 00:12:18.785
By the way, I got a new co-pilot for you.

133
00:12:19.202 --> 00:12:22.873
Last test, Carlos pissed hot. Coke.

134
00:12:23.457 --> 00:12:24.875
I mean, I reckon
he wanted to get busted.

135
00:12:24.958 --> 00:12:26.376
You saw how he was shaking.

136
00:12:26.877 --> 00:12:30.297
It was classic burn-out.
You burn out at 24.

137
00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.966
I mean, when I was 24,
burn-out hadn't been invented yet.

138
00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:34.301
Is that her there?

139
00:12:34.384 --> 00:12:36.636
Yeah, I know she looks like
a fucking child.

140
00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:39.431
But she's got 500 hours in Reapers,
100 in Predators.

141
00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.184
Top recruit from Holloman.

142
00:12:42.267 --> 00:12:45.937
Listen, word's come down the chain
we're stepping up attacks.

143
00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.857
'Cause we got intel that says
they're stepping up attacks.

144
00:12:49.316 --> 00:12:50.692
I mean, it's like my football coach
used to say,

145
00:12:50.776 --> 00:12:52.527
"Get your retaliation in first."

146
00:12:55.572 --> 00:12:56.782
What's up?

147
00:12:57.407 --> 00:12:59.076
Can you get me in a plane, sir?

148
00:13:00.952 --> 00:13:03.752
- You not hear what I was just saying?
- No, I heard you. I was just...

149
00:13:03.789 --> 00:13:06.458
They're yanking you jet jockeys
out of your kites faster than ever.

150
00:13:06.541 --> 00:13:10.379
I know how you feel. It's like going from
