151
00:13:11.671 --> 00:13:13.590
You think any of us love flying at 1-G?

152
00:13:16.385 --> 00:13:18.762
All right, I'll see what I can do. Okay?

153
00:13:18.845 --> 00:13:20.430
- Thank you, sir.
- All right.

154
00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.603
Not a word, Drier.
I can't have Egan burn out on me.

155
00:13:26.686 --> 00:13:29.064
I need someone
who can fly these fucking dodos.

156
00:13:30.941 --> 00:13:35.362
How can you feel turbulence hit a plane
7,000 miles away? It's un-fucking-canny.

157
00:13:36.071 --> 00:13:38.865
Everyone else is trying to act like
they're in a plane in Afghanistan.

158
00:13:38.949 --> 00:13:41.451
Egan fucking is in a plane
in Afghanistan.

159
00:13:49.126 --> 00:13:50.544
Suarez, go in tighter.

160
00:13:54.589 --> 00:13:57.926
Fuel window closing. Can't wait
for Johnny Jihad to make a pit stop.

161
00:13:58.051 --> 00:13:59.291
No, I can take him on the move.

162
00:13:59.553 --> 00:14:01.471
- Old Predator, Tommy.
- What's the lag?

163
00:14:02.139 --> 00:14:03.682
Latency at 2.2 seconds.

164
00:14:05.809 --> 00:14:08.728
How do you know where he's gonna be
two seconds from now, sir?

165
00:14:08.812 --> 00:14:10.439
You don't throw the ball
where the receiver is.

166
00:14:10.522 --> 00:14:11.982
You throw where he's gonna be.

167
00:14:12.065 --> 00:14:13.191
Lead them by a cross hair.

168
00:14:18.447 --> 00:14:20.198
One Minnesota, two Minnesota...

169
00:14:21.366 --> 00:14:23.243
Isn't it supposed to be Mississippi, sir?

170
00:14:23.326 --> 00:14:24.661
I'm from St. Paul.

171
00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:26.496
Lead them by another half.

172
00:14:30.375 --> 00:14:31.835
We are cleared hot.

173
00:14:31.918 --> 00:14:34.588
Master arm on. Weapon's hot.

174
00:14:35.505 --> 00:14:39.176
Three, two, one, rifle.

175
00:14:40.302 --> 00:14:41.845
Time of flight, 12 seconds.

176
00:14:53.064 --> 00:14:54.107
Yes!

177
00:14:54.191 --> 00:14:55.692
Got them motherfuckers.

178
00:14:56.359 --> 00:14:57.360
Good splash.

179
00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:03.783
- Tarfu.
- Tarfu? What's tarfu, sir?

180
00:15:03.867 --> 00:15:05.076
Totally and royally fucked up.

181
00:15:06.786 --> 00:15:08.788
And I believe those gentlemen qualify.

182
00:15:09.623 --> 00:15:10.665
Thank you, sir.

183
00:15:10.999 --> 00:15:12.959
So she's looking at me
and I'm looking at her, right?

184
00:15:13.043 --> 00:15:16.087
So, finally I decide I'm gonna go over
and introduce myself to her.

185
00:15:16.171 --> 00:15:19.132
And I say,
"Hi, I'm Captain Joseph Zimmer."

186
00:15:19.216 --> 00:15:20.550
- Nice.
- You know what she says?

187
00:15:20.926 --> 00:15:23.386
She says her name is Anita Mann.

188
00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:24.930
- It's funny.
- Yeah.

189
00:15:25.013 --> 00:15:26.473
Well, she was shitfaced, of course.

190
00:15:26.556 --> 00:15:28.850
At a bar at Mandalay Bay
with five of her girlfriends.

191
00:15:28.934 --> 00:15:30.644
She can't get me upstairs fast enough.

192
00:15:31.269 --> 00:15:34.564
The girl was getting married
the next fucking day.

193
00:15:35.315 --> 00:15:38.318
Last bachelor party I went to,
I was Dick Burns.

194
00:15:38.401 --> 00:15:39.761
It was either that or Hugh Jorgen.

195
00:15:41.238 --> 00:15:42.322
Classy.

196
00:15:49.663 --> 00:15:52.082
- So, did you volunteer?
- Or were you "volun-told"?

197
00:15:53.416 --> 00:15:57.254
I went willingly.
Yeah, I couldn't wait to sign up.

198
00:15:57.337 --> 00:16:00.799
Come on, battlefields and blackjack?
Every girl's fantasy.

199
00:16:01.758 --> 00:16:02.759
<i>You'?</i>

200
00:16:02.842 --> 00:16:04.842
In my line,
this is the next best thing to Langley.

201
00:16:05.387 --> 00:16:08.932
I applied twice, but I never got past
the background check.

202
00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:11.685
For the life of me,
I don't know what it is.

203
00:16:11.768 --> 00:16:14.437
I don't remember doing anything
that fucking bad.

204
00:16:14.604 --> 00:16:18.942
I flew cargo, Globemasters.
I might as well be working for UPS.

205
00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:22.790
If you want to be where the action is,
this is the tip of the spear.

206
00:16:30.579 --> 00:16:31.663
I did six tours.

207
00:16:33.748 --> 00:16:38.211
After the last one, I got back from Iraq,
a row of GCS's on the tarmac.

208
00:16:38.295 --> 00:16:40.005
F-16s in mothballs.

209
00:16:41.089 --> 00:16:43.383
Put in one UAV tour, they said.

210
00:16:44.676 --> 00:16:45.802
I'm on my third.

211
00:16:48.888 --> 00:16:50.473
You got a family.

212
00:16:50.557 --> 00:16:52.726
Must be nice, you know,
go home and see them every day.

213
00:16:55.645 --> 00:16:56.855
We're on duty.

214
00:17:15.165 --> 00:17:16.958
Where superpowers go to die.

215
00:17:18.668 --> 00:17:22.339
Not the British, not the Soviets, not us.

216
00:17:22.797 --> 00:17:26.343
Genghis fucking Khan
couldn't hold onto this fucking place.

217
00:17:28.178 --> 00:17:30.555
No one wins a war in Afghanistan.

218
00:17:31.222 --> 00:17:35.268
The only way to win is never put a boot
on the ground. Stay two miles above it.

219
00:17:35.352 --> 00:17:38.980
We have put in 600 Reaper hours
on this target, sir.

220
00:17:39.814 --> 00:17:44.486
May I respectfully suggest
that we got the wrong address?

221
00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:47.697
That's not what our intel's saying, Major.

222
00:17:47.781 --> 00:17:49.407
It's a safe house
for the new Number Two.

223
00:17:54.871 --> 00:17:55.872
Who's she?

224
00:17:55.955 --> 00:17:59.501
Our intel says she's not related.
Housekeeper.

225
00:17:59.918 --> 00:18:01.586
I always think they can see us.

226
00:18:02.545 --> 00:18:06.716
At 10,000 feet, even if she stared
straight at us, she couldn't see us.

227
00:18:08.176 --> 00:18:10.178
I get tired just watching her work.

228
00:18:10.303 --> 00:18:13.098
My wife by the fucking pool,
she wouldn't last a day over there.

229
00:18:38.373 --> 00:18:40.959
- He's getting good.
- Focus on the compound.

230
00:18:55.056 --> 00:18:57.517
Well, as much as I would like to
watch her put her son to sleep,

231
00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.519
I gotta be home before my kids wake up.

232
00:18:59.602 --> 00:19:01.938
- It's all yours, Major.
- Yeah. Good night, sir.

233
00:19:21.082 --> 00:19:23.543
- Is that the target?
- No.

234
00:19:24.836 --> 00:19:26.296
Our target's as round as he is tall.

235
00:19:26.379 --> 00:19:27.797
That's not him.

236
00:19:49.027 --> 00:19:50.653
What is he doing?

237
00:19:53.823 --> 00:19:54.908
Shit.

238
00:20:04.959 --> 00:20:05.960
Jesus.

239
00:21:11.901 --> 00:21:13.069
Hey, Tommy.

240
00:21:17.574 --> 00:21:19.784
So, I heard you want to
go back to combat.

241
00:21:24.455 --> 00:21:25.790
You told Molly yet?

242
00:21:28.126 --> 00:21:29.377
Not yet.

243
00:21:29.836 --> 00:21:32.297
Well, don't take this the wrong way,

244
00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:34.173
but are you out of your fucking mind?

245
00:21:35.383 --> 00:21:37.010
I mean, look around, buddy.

246
00:21:37.594 --> 00:21:40.013
We can come home at night.
We can see our kids,

247
