00:39:21.531 --> 00:39:25.535
<i>Al-Qaeda's number one bomb maker
will never again harm one of us.</i>

491
00:39:29.373 --> 00:39:31.166
<i>Please do a follow-up.</i>

492
00:39:34.336 --> 00:39:37.005
Did I hear you correctly, Langley?

493
00:39:38.298 --> 00:39:40.634
<i>There are other combatants
in the vicinity.</i>

494
00:39:42.177 --> 00:39:43.261
Double tap?

495
00:39:43.428 --> 00:39:45.555
<i>We prefer the term "follow-up."</i>

496
00:39:45.681 --> 00:39:46.807
Sir...

497
00:39:49.434 --> 00:39:51.228
They are rescuers. We can't...

498
00:39:51.311 --> 00:39:52.711
The fuck we can't. They're Taliban.

499
00:39:52.771 --> 00:39:55.190
Who do you think the first responders
are gonna be, Quakers?

500
00:39:55.983 --> 00:39:57.985
Those rescuers have RPGs.

501
00:40:01.363 --> 00:40:05.450
- I see people with shovels.
- Then just hit the ones with the RPGs.

502
00:40:10.414 --> 00:40:12.624
Can you confirm that order, Langley?

503
00:40:12.708 --> 00:40:15.460
<i>In our opinion, it's proportionate.</i>

504
00:40:16.962 --> 00:40:19.548
Sir, forgive me, sir.
What the hell does that mean?

505
00:40:19.631 --> 00:40:23.260
<i>It means that in our assessment,
the combatants we are targeting</i>

506
00:40:23.343 --> 00:40:26.304
<i>pose a grave-enough threat
to the United States</i>

507
00:40:26.388 --> 00:40:29.641
<i>to justify potential civilian casualties.</i>

508
00:40:29.725 --> 00:40:34.104
<i>Not to mention that this pre-emptive
self-defense is approved and ordered</i>

509
00:40:34.187 --> 00:40:36.106
<i>by the administration.</i>

510
00:40:36.231 --> 00:40:37.774
<i>Please engage.</i>

511
00:40:38.984 --> 00:40:40.193
Orders.

512
00:40:48.535 --> 00:40:51.371
- Laser.
- Lasing.

513
00:40:53.790 --> 00:40:56.501
Master arm on. Weapon's hot.

514
00:41:01.798 --> 00:41:04.760
Three, two, one, rifle.

515
00:41:05.677 --> 00:41:08.430
Weapon's away.
Time of flight, 10 seconds.

516
00:41:26.782 --> 00:41:29.785
Master arm off.

517
00:41:37.709 --> 00:41:39.669
<i>The subject on the left,</i>

518
00:41:41.296 --> 00:41:42.964
<i>what is she doing?</i>

519
00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:47.219
I believe she's picking
an arm off a tree, sir.

520
00:41:49.888 --> 00:41:52.182
Would they like me to do
further damage assessment?

521
00:41:55.268 --> 00:41:56.478
Hand it off, Tommy.

522
00:41:57.145 --> 00:41:59.481
Captain Christie, take the controls.

523
00:42:08.323 --> 00:42:11.493
Damage assessment, estimate, 12.

524
00:42:14.246 --> 00:42:16.039
Well, we count...

525
00:42:16.748 --> 00:42:18.583
Twelve dead, Langley.

526
00:42:18.667 --> 00:42:20.168
Give or take.

527
00:42:21.753 --> 00:42:24.172
<i>We concur. Signing off.</i>

528
00:42:27.968 --> 00:42:29.761
Was that a war crime, sir?

529
00:42:29.845 --> 00:42:31.847
Shut the fuck up, Suarez.

530
00:42:32.472 --> 00:42:35.433
How'd they decide
the condolence payment is five K?

531
00:42:35.767 --> 00:42:37.686
Sounds like a lot to me.

532
00:42:38.270 --> 00:42:40.313
You could live there on,
like, a dollar a day.

533
00:42:44.151 --> 00:42:45.610
What was that shit?

534
00:42:48.029 --> 00:42:49.698
I didn't sign up for that shit.

535
00:42:50.407 --> 00:42:52.909
That's what terrorists do.
You know that, right?

536
00:42:53.952 --> 00:42:57.205
Plant a second bomb, blow up soldiers
showing up for the first bomb.

537
00:42:58.665 --> 00:43:00.167
Since when did we become Hamas?

538
00:43:04.546 --> 00:43:06.298
"Approved by the administration."

539
00:43:07.841 --> 00:43:09.759
They give Nobel Peace Prizes
for this now?

540
00:43:09.843 --> 00:43:11.178
They sure do.

541
00:43:13.722 --> 00:43:15.682
You wanna talk about all the shots
we didn't take,

542
00:43:15.724 --> 00:43:18.310
waiting for some D.C. lawyer
to come back from lunch?

543
00:43:20.187 --> 00:43:22.480
- No wonder they hate us.
- They always hated us.

544
00:43:22.564 --> 00:43:26.318
We're always gonna be the great Satan
because we got Hustler and Hooters,

545
00:43:26.401 --> 00:43:28.153
and we let women drive
and go to school.

546
00:43:28.236 --> 00:43:30.530
And they're not gonna stop hating us
until the savages

547
00:43:30.614 --> 00:43:33.158
have Sharia law everywhere
on the goddamn planet.

548
00:43:33.700 --> 00:43:35.785
You think you'd have this job
if you were over there?

549
00:43:35.869 --> 00:43:37.871
- Do you think you'd have any job?
- There were kids!

550
00:43:37.954 --> 00:43:39.539
Not our fault. They shouldn't
bring kids into a war zone.

551
00:43:39.623 --> 00:43:40.665
They live there!

552
00:43:40.749 --> 00:43:43.001
Did you get the wrong address, Suarez?

553
00:43:43.752 --> 00:43:46.671
Look around you.
This is a military base. It's what we do.

554
00:43:46.922 --> 00:43:48.965
We're fighting a war
and we're winning it.

555
00:43:49.049 --> 00:43:50.508
They bomb New York lately?

556
00:43:51.134 --> 00:43:54.971
We're saving American lives.
So, fucking sue me.

557
00:43:59.643 --> 00:44:00.769
God is great.

558
00:44:01.937 --> 00:44:03.271
Later, Jane Fonda.

559
00:44:03.855 --> 00:44:06.816
You're a fucking idiot, Zimmer.
No offense.

560
00:44:07.400 --> 00:44:09.069
Actually, offense.

561
00:44:11.821 --> 00:44:13.615
What do you think, sir?

562
00:44:14.282 --> 00:44:16.952
- Those are the orders.
- Yeah.

563
00:44:20.288 --> 00:44:21.915
At least it doesn't give you a hard-on.

564
00:44:23.124 --> 00:44:26.461
Sorry, sir, I could just...
I could kill Zimmer.

565
00:44:28.296 --> 00:44:30.131
Death Junkie Christie.

566
00:44:32.801 --> 00:44:34.469
We should go out on the town.

567
00:44:40.058 --> 00:44:41.601
You know, just our crew.

568
00:44:43.228 --> 00:44:45.897
So we don't end up killing each other
in that goddamn sweatbox.

569
00:44:54.489 --> 00:44:55.532
- Hi, Dad.
- Hi, Daddy!

570
00:44:55.615 --> 00:44:56.741
Hey.

571
00:44:56.825 --> 00:44:58.493
All right, come on. Get in the car.

572
00:44:59.786 --> 00:45:00.954
No pushing.

573
00:45:09.129 --> 00:45:11.256
What's the Pythagorean theorem?

574
00:45:11.339 --> 00:45:15.385
The square of the hypotenuse
is equal to the sum

575
00:45:15.468 --> 00:45:18.513
of the squares on the other two sides.

576
00:45:18.596 --> 00:45:20.223
There you go. Nicely done.

577
00:45:22.559 --> 00:45:24.644
Did you really need to know
all this to be a pilot?

578
00:45:24.728 --> 00:45:27.188
Absolutely not.
They said I did, but I didn't.

579
00:45:27.355 --> 00:45:29.232
Still, it's good to know it anyway.

580
00:45:50.420 --> 00:45:52.339
The truck's making that noise again.

581
00:45:54.049 --> 00:45:55.925
I'm gonna need to take it to the shop.

582
00:45:56.009 --> 00:45:59.971
All right, well, I'll take a look at it.
Those guys will rip you off.

583
00:46:00.138 --> 00:46:01.222
Okay.

584
00:46:21.326 --> 00:46:22.952
To Crew 3-2.

585
00:46:28.708 --> 00:46:29.918
Fucking Vegas.

586
00:46:31.628 --> 00:46:33.588
You wanna see how civilization ends,
come here.

587
00:46:34.255 --> 00:46:39.135
Caesars Palace, New York-New York,
Paris, The Venetian, Monte Carlo...

588
00:46:39.761 --> 00:46:42.263
- What's the goddamn pyramid?
- Luxor.

589
00:46:42.430 --> 00:46:44.724
No wonder fuck-all Americans
got a passport.

590
00:46:45.266 --> 00:46:47.060
They think the world's all here.

591
00:46:47.685 --> 00:46:48.978
End of civilization.

592
00:46:50.271 --> 00:46:53.233
Who's up for a lap dance, huh?
I'm paying.

593
00:46:53.316 --> 00:46:55.652
- Really?
- No, I'm not.

594
00:46:56.277 --> 00:46:57.362
Dick.

595
00:47:09.541 --> 00:47:11.021
You and your wife
from somewhere else?

596
00:47:12.127 --> 00:47:14.838
I've never met anyone in Vegas
that actually comes from here.

597
00:47:14.921 --> 00:47:16.881
Well, she does.

598
00:47:16.965 --> 00:47:18.883
I met her when she was working
at the Tropicana

599
00:47:18.967 --> 00:47:22.429
about a year before I shipped out
to the sandbox, my last tour.

600
00:47:24.305 --> 00:47:27.767
First date, I took her flying in an F-16.

601
00:47:28.643 --> 00:47:30.061
- That'll work.
- Yeah.

602
00:47:30.145 --> 00:47:33.565
She thought I was exciting
in a boring kind of way.

603
00:47:33.648 --> 00:47:37.444
And a part of her just liked
Uncle's paychecks every 15 days.

604
00:47:38.653 --> 00:47:40.196
What about you?

605
00:47:40.947 --> 00:47:44.033
Battlefields and blackjack?
Still every girl's dream?

606
00:47:44.909 --> 00:47:45.910
I don't know.

607
00:47:49.998 --> 00:47:51.749
How bad do you miss it?

608
00:47:54.210 --> 00:47:55.712
Flying.

609
00:47:58.339 --> 00:47:59.799
I miss the fear.

610
00:48:01.176 --> 00:48:04.304
You're up in the sky,
something can happen.

611
00:48:05.138 --> 00:48:06.931
There's a risk, you know?

612
00:48:07.015 --> 00:48:12.312
I mean, try landing on a carrier
at night or in rough seas,

613
00:48:12.687 --> 00:48:15.690
the deck's pitching 30 feet, low fuel.

614
00:48:18.526 --> 00:48:20.612
We've got no skin in the game.

615
00:48:22.155 --> 00:48:25.492
I feel like a coward every day.

616
00:48:26.534 --> 00:48:31.456
Taking pot shots from half a world away
in an air-conditioned cubicle.

617
00:48:31.581 --> 00:48:36.252
I mean, they get lucky, they shoot
my plane down. I'm not even in it.

618
00:48:36.336 --> 00:48:38.421
All we got to do is
pull another one out of the box.

619
00:48:39.881 --> 00:48:44.010
Worst thing that can happen to me is
carpal tunnel or I spill coffee in my lap.

620
00:48:44.385 --> 00:48:48.556
The most dangerous thing I do
is drive home on the freeway.

621
00:48:53.520 --> 00:48:56.523
Yeah, I get the feeling
I'm gonna die of boredom.

622
00:49:05.114 --> 00:49:08.785
Well, I'm gonna try my luck.

623
00:49:09.619 --> 00:49:11.371
Yeah. All right.

624
00:49:13.915 --> 00:49:14.958
<i>You'?</i>

625
00:49:16.334 --> 00:49:18.503
No, I'd better get going. I got...

626
00:49:23.424 --> 00:49:24.425
Okay.

627
00:49:25.593 --> 00:49:27.262
- Good night, sir.
- Good night.

628
00:49:54.289 --> 00:49:55.290
Fuck.

629
00:50:02.797 --> 00:50:04.424
- Major.
- Yeah.

630
00:50:05.592 --> 00:50:08.303
You in a hurry?
You might want to throttle back.

631
00:50:09.637 --> 00:50:10.847
Yeah, no, I was...

632
00:50:11.598 --> 00:50:12.932
Yeah, I don't know.

633
00:50:21.149 --> 00:50:22.275
Listen, Major...

634
00:50:25.153 --> 00:50:26.487
I'm a vet.

635
00:50:34.329 --> 00:50:35.997
I'll let it slide this one time.

636
00:50:37.540 --> 00:50:39.167
Come on, I'll get you home safe.

637
00:50:50.637 --> 00:50:53.056
Hey, Jesse, what are you doing awake?

638
00:50:53.139 --> 00:50:54.390
I'm thinking.

639
00:50:55.183 --> 00:50:56.517
Well, what you thinking about?

640
00:50:56.934 --> 00:50:59.562
- Everything.
- Well, that's a lot to be thinking about.

641
00:50:59.687 --> 00:51:02.023
Why don't you try
just thinking about sleeping?

642
00:51:02.106 --> 00:51:03.858
I'll do that.

643
00:51:03.941 --> 00:51:05.360
Good night, Daddy.

644
00:51:49.737 --> 00:51:51.739
We made the papers again.

645
00:51:54.659 --> 00:51:58.287
Ever notice when they burn Old Glory,
their flags are always homemade?

646
00:51:58.913 --> 00:52:01.194
For some reason, they don't stock
the Star-Spangled Banner

647
00:52:01.249 --> 00:52:03.167
in those Pashtun bazaars. No.

648
00:52:04.293 --> 00:52:07.880
Somebody had to paint
these 50 stars and 13 bars by hand.

649
00:52:07.964 --> 00:52:09.124
They had to do it just right.

650
00:52:10.800 --> 00:52:14.220
So we definitely know it's us
that's got them so upset.

651
00:52:17.432 --> 00:52:20.560
Like some guy stayed up all night
making that symbol of

652
00:52:20.643 --> 00:52:23.271
evil American imperialism
just as good as he can.

653
00:52:25.940 --> 00:52:28.192
A lot of love went into that hate.

654
00:52:30.570 --> 00:52:32.363
I've never been to Yemen, sir.

655
00:52:34.240 --> 00:52:36.367
If I were you, I'd keep it that way.

656
00:52:44.333 --> 00:52:47.837
This is Johns. We're over
your requested position, Langley.

657
00:52:47.962 --> 00:52:51.215
These are the coordinates
for Al-Bayda province, South Yemen.

658
00:52:51.299 --> 00:52:53.551
<i>Good afternoon,
Lieutenant Colonel Johns.</i>

659
00:52:53.634 --> 00:52:56.471
Last time I checked, Langley,
we're not at war with Yemen.

660
00:52:58.097 --> 00:53:01.517
<i>While we respect state sovereignty
and the rule of law, Colonel,</i>

661
00:53:01.642 --> 00:53:04.228
<i>we're regrettably facing
a substate adversary</i>

662
00:53:04.312 --> 00:53:05.855
<i>who abides by no rules.</i>

663
00:53:06.355 --> 00:53:10.109
<i>Out of necessity, this war on terror
has become borderless.</i>

664
00:53:11.319 --> 00:53:14.280
<i>The target is the Al-Qaeda cell
gathered by the market.</i>

665
00:53:19.494 --> 00:53:20.620
We see the crowd.

666
00:53:25.666 --> 00:53:27.502
You want us to kill a crowd?

667
00:53:28.085 --> 00:53:31.714
<i>Al-Qaeda unsurprisingly,
tend to congregate with Al-Qaeda</i>

668
00:53:31.839 --> 00:53:33.674
<i>or associated forces.</i>

669
00:53:34.675 --> 00:53:38.471
<i>Consequently, we've determined
that it is militarily more effective</i>

670
00:53:38.554 --> 00:53:41.307
<i>to eliminate a group than an individual.</i>

671
00:53:53.611 --> 00:53:55.446
Does that include the underage boy, sir?

672
00:53:55.530 --> 00:53:59.367
<i>Our analysts see only
military age males.</i>

673
00:53:59.450 --> 00:54:04.705
<i>In our assessment, this Al-Qaeda cell
represents an imminent threat.</i>

674
00:54:06.541 --> 00:54:08.584
<i>Permission to prosecute.</i>

675
00:54:08.960 --> 00:54:10.503
<i>Please cease recording.</i>

676
00:54:22.890 --> 00:54:25.852
- Laser.
- Lasing.

677
00:54:25.935 --> 00:54:29.063
Master arm on, weapon's hot.

678
00:54:30.523 --> 00:54:33.401
Three, two, one...

679
00:54:34.402 --> 00:54:35.862
Rifle.

680
00:54:36.946 --> 00:54:39.490
Missiles away. Time of flight,

681
00:54:40.449 --> 00:54:41.826
ten seconds.

682
00:54:58.759 --> 00:55:00.595
Like fish in a fucking barrel.

683
00:55:01.721 --> 00:55:05.683
<i>It is a sad fact that
war is often asymmetrical.</i>

684
00:55:06.225 --> 00:55:09.604
<i>Please forego damage assessment
and exit the airspace.</i>

685
00:55:16.611 --> 00:55:18.905
Master arm off, weapon's safe.

686
00:55:19.113 --> 00:55:20.323
Laser's safe.

687
00:55:31.542 --> 00:55:34.420
"Imminent threat"? They couldn't live
any further away from us.

688
00:55:35.212 --> 00:55:38.132
- Poorest fucking place on earth.
- Setting the course for Djibouti.

689
00:55:38.466 --> 00:55:40.301
It depends on
your definition of imminent.

690
00:55:42.511 --> 00:55:44.305
Actually, you're right about that.

691
00:55:45.264 --> 00:55:46.390
- I am?
- Yeah.

692
00:55:46.474 --> 00:55:49.393
Take a while for that boy to get big
enough to hold a Kalashnikov.

693
00:55:49.477 --> 00:55:53.022
But no question, we are a regular
fucking terrorist factory.

694
00:55:53.314 --> 00:55:55.816
Best recruitment tool
Al-Qaeda ever had.

695
00:55:55.900 --> 00:55:57.740
We can kill them faster
than they can make 'em.

696
00:55:57.818 --> 00:56:00.099
Fuck you, Zimmer.
You'd better pray they never get drones.

697
00:56:00.154 --> 00:56:01.714
They're not gonna
waste money on a drone

698
00:56:01.739 --> 00:56:03.908
when they can strap a bomb to a kid.

699
00:56:03.991 --> 00:56:06.410
Did you know the Times Square bomber
was trained in Yemen?

700
00:56:06.494 --> 00:56:08.579
Not very well. It didn't go off.

701
00:56:08.663 --> 00:56:09.705
Asshole.

702
00:56:09.997 --> 00:56:13.417
The reason he tried to blow us up

703
00:56:13.501 --> 00:56:15.086
was drone strikes.

704
00:56:15.169 --> 00:56:18.297
So obviously we should keep on
hitting them with drone strikes, right?

705
00:56:18.965 --> 00:56:20.007
Yes.

706
00:56:24.303 --> 00:56:26.055
Prepare to hand off.

707
00:56:36.065 --> 00:56:37.233
- Hey, man.
- Hey, Zack.

708
00:56:45.199 --> 00:56:47.034
Major, we got a customer.

709
00:56:47.952 --> 00:56:51.205
- You're the only available crew.
- What is it?

710
00:56:51.914 --> 00:56:54.041
Overwatch. One-Six.

711
00:57:22.778 --> 00:57:25.156
Warhorse Six, this is Deadly Four-One.

712
00:57:26.240 --> 00:57:27.992
<i>Deadly Four-One,</i>

713
00:57:28.075 --> 00:57:31.162
<i>my men need some shuteye.
Can you watch our backs?</i>

714
00:57:31.245 --> 00:57:35.583
<i>Make sure we don't get
any uninvited guests till 0600?</i>

715
00:57:36.584 --> 00:57:38.252
That's an affirmative, Warhorse Six.

716
00:57:39.128 --> 00:57:41.756
I got fuel for six hours.

717
00:57:43.758 --> 00:57:45.551
There's nothing close to your position.

718
00:57:47.178 --> 00:57:49.597
<i>Roger that. Nice to hear.</i>

719
00:57:51.432 --> 00:57:52.600
Sleep tight.

720
00:57:55.853 --> 00:57:57.563
<i>Copy. Out.</i>

721
00:58:58.499 --> 00:58:59.708
Warhorse Six...

722
00:59:03.295 --> 00:59:05.339
This is Deadly Four-One.

723
00:59:06.924 --> 00:59:09.135
And this is your wake up call.

724
00:59:13.347 --> 00:59:17.059
<i>Roger that, Deadly Four-One.
We owe you.</i>

725
00:59:37.037 --> 00:59:38.706
Your appointment today...

726
00:59:40.916 --> 00:59:42.710
Was it life or death?

727
00:59:44.712 --> 00:59:46.380
Because mine was.

728
00:59:49.216 --> 00:59:50.551
That's cheap.

729
00:59:53.888 --> 00:59:55.389
You're right.

730
00:59:58.225 --> 00:59:59.727
I'm sorry.

731
01:00:02.897 --> 01:00:04.523
What was your appointment?

732
01:00:04.607 --> 01:00:08.068
If you must know,
I was going to go to a class at the gym.

733
01:00:08.694 --> 01:00:11.322
I was trying to stay in shape
in case I go back to dancing.

734
01:00:12.323 --> 01:00:13.908
Chorus like we talked about.

735
01:00:16.243 --> 01:00:17.912
I blew 50 bucks not going.

736
01:00:18.579 --> 01:00:21.207
I'm sorry.
I'll try to make soccer tomorrow.

737
01:00:21.749 --> 01:00:23.626
I will, Molly.

738
01:00:27.880 --> 01:00:30.007
I did something good today.

739
01:00:32.343 --> 01:00:34.011
You don't always?

740
01:00:37.473 --> 01:00:39.600
Let me make it up to you.

741
01:01:10.422 --> 01:01:11.882
Prepare to hand off.

742
01:01:13.300 --> 01:01:15.500
There's a man in Langley
who wants to borrow your plane.

743
01:01:16.679 --> 01:01:17.972
Handing off.

744
01:01:21.642 --> 01:01:25.562
Must be nice, Egan.
Hand-picked by the spooks,

745
01:01:25.646 --> 01:01:26.730
getting all the plum assignments.

746
01:01:26.814 --> 01:01:28.315
Is that what they are?

747
01:01:28.649 --> 01:01:32.069
Better than circling that compound like
some two-bit detective on a stakeout.

748
01:01:33.320 --> 01:01:35.948
- What's going on there?
- Nothing. That's the point.

749
01:01:36.031 --> 01:01:38.492
No, no, no. Right there. There.

750
01:01:39.868 --> 01:01:41.036
Same guy.

751
01:01:42.371 --> 01:01:43.455
Yup.

752
01:02:08.147 --> 01:02:09.481
He's a bad guy.

753
01:02:10.816 --> 01:02:12.860
He's just not our bad guy.

754
01:02:25.456 --> 01:02:26.874
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

755
01:02:36.091 --> 01:02:37.885
What's she doing now?

756
01:02:40.054 --> 01:02:41.722
She's going back to work.

757
01:02:51.231 --> 01:02:52.816
Major, we got new co-ords
from Langley.

758
01:02:53.817 --> 01:02:55.277
Sending them to you now.

759
01:03:00.532 --> 01:03:03.077
You ever seen
how beautiful it is in Virginia?

760
01:03:03.911 --> 01:03:06.497
It's green. It's not like here.

761
01:03:08.165 --> 01:03:12.252
You want to start a family,
crime in Virginia is non-existent.

762
01:03:13.921 --> 01:03:15.923
It's like heaven on earth.

763
01:03:40.531 --> 01:03:41.532
Hey.

764
01:03:49.540 --> 01:03:51.625
You want to go somewhere today

765
01:03:51.708 --> 01:03:54.086
- and do something?
- Yeah?

766
01:03:55.963 --> 01:03:57.256
It's strange.

767
01:03:58.715 --> 01:04:01.552
Imagine growing up
praying for gray skies.

768
01:04:02.469 --> 01:04:04.972
They hate blue skies
'cause that's when we fly.

769
01:04:05.681 --> 01:04:07.015
Gray skies, maybe not.

770
01:04:10.644 --> 01:04:11.979
Let's do something.

771
01:04:13.397 --> 01:04:14.815
Go to the strip...

772
01:04:16.316 --> 01:04:17.484
Or dancing?

773
01:04:29.329 --> 01:04:30.664
Splash.

774
01:04:32.374 --> 01:04:33.709
No, he's getting away.

775
01:04:46.638 --> 01:04:48.599
- Grenades.
- Withhold ordnance.

776
01:04:48.682 --> 01:04:50.893
They're not grenades,
Intelligence Coordinator Zimmer.

777
01:04:50.976 --> 01:04:52.352
They're fucking pomegranates.

778
01:04:55.647 --> 01:04:57.900
<i>Thanks for the cover, Cyclops 8.</i>

779
01:04:57.983 --> 01:04:59.693
<i>How's the weather in Vegas?</i>

780
01:04:59.776 --> 01:05:02.154
Hotter than hell here, Bronco Two.

781
01:05:02.237 --> 01:05:04.031
<i>Happy to trade places.</i>

782
01:05:07.743 --> 01:05:09.870
Shit! Shit, what was that?

783
01:05:10.037 --> 01:05:12.331
LED. He stepped on an IED.

784
01:05:12.414 --> 01:05:14.833
Shoot back! Shoot something.

785
01:06:31.952 --> 01:06:34.621
<i>Hey, it's Molly. I'm not here.
Have a great day.</i>

786
01:06:35.330 --> 01:06:37.291
Molly, call me back.

787
01:06:52.222 --> 01:06:54.391
He's using the fertilizer to grow things.

788
01:06:54.474 --> 01:06:57.603
The question is,
does he use it to kill things?

789
01:06:57.686 --> 01:07:00.981
And this is not
your usual Afghani cash crop.

790
01:07:01.648 --> 01:07:03.317
He's actually growing something to eat.

791
01:07:04.651 --> 01:07:06.737
<i>The traffic to and from the structure</i>

792
01:07:06.820 --> 01:07:09.156
<i>indicates to us the presence
of a bomb factory.</i>

793
01:07:11.116 --> 01:07:12.367
<i>In our judgment,</i>

794
01:07:12.451 --> 01:07:14.411
<i>the greater risk is to do nothing.</i>

795
01:07:16.455 --> 01:07:17.623
Roger that, Langley.

796
01:07:20.000 --> 01:07:21.168
Major.

797
01:07:25.339 --> 01:07:26.423
Major.

798
01:07:30.010 --> 01:07:32.763
- Yeah, laser on.
- It's lased, Major.

799
01:07:33.388 --> 01:07:36.183
Master arm on, weapon's hot.

800
01:07:36.391 --> 01:07:39.811
Three, two, one, rifle.

801
01:07:40.979 --> 01:07:43.607
Missile's away.
Time of flight, 10 seconds.

802
01:07:58.038 --> 01:07:59.331
Good kill.

803
01:08:09.716 --> 01:08:10.759
Hi.

804
01:08:13.136 --> 01:08:15.681
- I told you not to wait up.
- You drunk?

805
01:08:17.057 --> 01:08:18.433
That's rich coming from you.

806
01:08:18.517 --> 01:08:19.726
Where you been?

807
01:08:21.478 --> 01:08:23.689
I told you I was going out with the girls.

808
01:08:24.439 --> 01:08:25.857
What's wrong with you?

809
01:08:31.947 --> 01:08:34.366
Don't treat me like a damn fool.

810
01:08:35.742 --> 01:08:37.244
I saw you today...

811
01:08:39.037 --> 01:08:41.164
...in the truck with Danny.

812
01:08:41.248 --> 01:08:43.500
He was trying to work out
what's wrong with the truck.

813
01:08:45.252 --> 01:08:46.461
Because you never did.

814
01:08:48.839 --> 01:08:51.299
Plus I thought
it might be fun to blow him.

815
01:08:56.263 --> 01:08:57.889
I left you a message.

816
01:08:59.099 --> 01:09:00.475
My phone died.

817
01:09:01.685 --> 01:09:03.103
I just got your messages.

818
01:09:03.729 --> 01:09:06.106
- Let me see your phone.
- No.

819
01:09:12.529 --> 01:09:13.822
Give me your phone.

820
01:09:24.583 --> 01:09:26.042
Why'd you change your password?

821
01:09:27.878 --> 01:09:29.713
Because the kids know it

822
01:09:29.796 --> 01:09:31.631
and they're always
fucking with my phone.

823
01:09:32.841 --> 01:09:33.884
Give me the new password.

824
01:09:34.885 --> 01:09:36.344
It's Tommy.

825
01:09:37.971 --> 01:09:39.055
Tommy.

826
01:09:47.105 --> 01:09:48.398
But I'll change that now.

827
01:09:54.654 --> 01:09:56.239
You think I'm having an affair.

828
01:10:00.243 --> 01:10:01.495
You know, I...

829
01:10:02.037 --> 01:10:03.830
I've thought about it.

830
01:10:05.332 --> 01:10:08.585
And you know what else,
I don't think it would even be cheating.

831
01:10:08.668 --> 01:10:11.213
Because to cheat on someone,
you'd have to be in a relationship.

832
01:10:12.506 --> 01:10:14.257
And I don't know that we are anymore.

833
01:10:14.341 --> 01:10:15.842
If that's what helps you.

834
01:10:16.843 --> 01:10:18.178
Bet that helps.

835
01:10:20.222 --> 01:10:21.807
What is this about?

836
01:10:21.890 --> 01:10:24.450
I mean, is this really just about you
losing a seat in the plane?

837
01:10:26.812 --> 01:10:29.105
'Cause here's your last piece
of truth for the day.

838
01:10:29.481 --> 01:10:31.900
Nobody is gonna put you back in one.

839
01:10:36.321 --> 01:10:38.365
But I wasn't the one
that drug you out of the fucking thing,

840
01:10:38.448 --> 01:10:40.367
so taking it out on me
isn't going to help.

841
01:10:42.619 --> 01:10:44.120
And you were right about one thing.

842
01:10:44.830 --> 01:10:46.039
Yeah, what's that?

843
01:10:46.414 --> 01:10:49.084
At least when you were away,
you were really away.

844
01:10:49.167 --> 01:10:51.378
Now you're here, but fuck it.

845
01:10:53.213 --> 01:10:54.548
But what?

846
01:10:55.257 --> 01:10:58.885
What is it that you need so bad?
What is it that you miss so bad?

847
01:10:59.553 --> 01:11:02.097
Combat? You miss the fucking combat?

848
01:11:02.597 --> 01:11:05.183
Hit me. Hit me, you like that.

849
01:11:05.267 --> 01:11:07.936
- I hit you one time. Will you stop?
- Come on, you little bitch! Hit me.

850
01:11:08.019 --> 01:11:09.688
- Hit me, little bitch, hit me!
- Molly, don't do that!

851
01:11:09.771 --> 01:11:12.107
- Hit me!
- Molly. Molly! Just stop it, all right.

852
01:11:13.066 --> 01:11:16.903
Fuck! Fuck! Fuck! Fuck!

853
01:11:19.948 --> 01:11:21.116
It's okay.

854
01:11:23.451 --> 01:11:24.578
Fuck!

855
01:13:27.701 --> 01:13:29.661
<i>Langley, signing Off-</i>

856
01:14:16.041 --> 01:14:17.250
Seriously, dude...

857
01:14:18.543 --> 01:14:21.421
It's not like a costume you rent
when you wanna get lucky or...

858
01:15:27.821 --> 01:15:28.988
Hey.

859
01:15:30.490 --> 01:15:31.491
Hey.

860
01:15:41.167 --> 01:15:42.502
You look miles away.

861
01:15:44.546 --> 01:15:45.755
Seven thousand.

862
01:15:50.927 --> 01:15:53.054
You wanna know about my job?

863
01:15:54.681 --> 01:15:55.765
Yeah.

864
01:15:56.599 --> 01:15:57.809
Well...

865
01:15:59.686 --> 01:16:04.065
Yesterday, I was flying over a house
in South Waziristan.

866
01:16:07.318 --> 01:16:08.987
It was night when I started watching

867
01:16:09.070 --> 01:16:11.322
but they couldn't see me
even if it was day.

868
01:16:14.701 --> 01:16:17.036
It was the house of
a Taliban commander.

869
01:16:18.538 --> 01:16:19.789
He wasn't home.

870
01:16:21.332 --> 01:16:24.294
Inside his wife and family were sleeping.

871
01:16:24.711 --> 01:16:28.715
When he did come back around dawn,
the family was still inside,

872
01:16:28.798 --> 01:16:31.676
but I wasn't sure
when I'd get this chance again so...

873
01:16:33.011 --> 01:16:35.013
I blew the house up anyway.

874
01:16:43.396 --> 01:16:44.439
And I watched

875
01:16:46.316 --> 01:16:49.068
as the neighbors started
pulling the bodies out.

876
01:16:52.906 --> 01:16:56.034
Another one of my jobs
is damage assessment,

877
01:16:57.410 --> 01:16:59.329
which is our way of saying
counting the dead,

878
01:16:59.412 --> 01:17:02.248
which is not as easy as it sounds.

879
01:17:03.374 --> 01:17:06.544
Because a lot of times the bodies
are in such small pieces.

880
01:17:08.087 --> 01:17:11.382
But this time, I knew for sure

881
01:17:12.550 --> 01:17:13.927
it was seven.

882
01:17:15.595 --> 01:17:19.098
<i>I watched all morning
as these locals cleaned up the mess,</i>

883
01:17:20.141 --> 01:17:22.227
<i>got ready for the funeral.</i>

884
01:17:24.687 --> 01:17:27.232
<i>They like to bury their dead
within 24 hours.</i>

885
01:17:29.275 --> 01:17:32.987
Which is a happy coincidence for me

886
01:17:33.071 --> 01:17:35.573
because that's how long
I can stay in the air.

887
01:17:37.909 --> 01:17:39.452
I watched them

888
01:17:40.286 --> 01:17:43.539
carry the bodies
up a hill to the gravesite.

889
01:17:44.540 --> 01:17:47.126
I had information
that the Taliban commander's brother

890
01:17:47.252 --> 01:17:48.920
<i>would attend the funeral.</i>

891
01:17:49.796 --> 01:17:52.799
<i>So, I waited</i>

892
01:17:53.925 --> 01:17:55.885
<i>till they were all there</i>

893
01:17:57.303 --> 01:17:58.680
saying their prayers.

894
01:18:06.479 --> 01:18:08.231
And then I blew them up, too.

895
01:18:35.425 --> 01:18:36.676
That's my job.

896
01:19:49.582 --> 01:19:50.833
Come inside.

897
01:19:52.585 --> 01:19:54.295
I need you to come inside.

898
01:19:56.672 --> 01:19:58.091
Get back in the house.

899
01:20:00.927 --> 01:20:03.763
It's so beautifully clear
when we watch them.

900
01:20:04.680 --> 01:20:07.266
It couldn't be clearer if I was there.

901
01:20:09.811 --> 01:20:13.731
You can see everything,
the looks on their faces, everything.

902
01:20:15.942 --> 01:20:17.443
Tommy, please.

903
01:20:20.947 --> 01:20:22.615
Once you see it,

904
01:20:23.741 --> 01:20:25.201
how do you unsee it?

905
01:20:28.955 --> 01:20:30.373
You call in sick.

906
01:20:30.790 --> 01:20:32.291
You need help.

907
01:20:32.708 --> 01:20:34.460
You shouldn't be driving a car,
let alone...

908
01:20:34.544 --> 01:20:36.212
No, I'm okay. I'm okay.

909
01:20:36.796 --> 01:20:39.006
- No, you can't go!
- I'm okay.

910
01:20:39.090 --> 01:20:40.758
No!

911
01:21:31.517 --> 01:21:33.811
- Cutting it close.
- Yeah, well, I made it, didn't I?

912
01:21:35.605 --> 01:21:37.773
- Need some gum, sir?
- No.

913
01:21:40.860 --> 01:21:43.696
No, you need some gum, sir.

914
01:21:53.372 --> 01:21:56.667
- Starting early. You okay?
- Yeah.

915
01:21:56.876 --> 01:21:58.169
Christie can cover for you.

916
01:22:01.297 --> 01:22:02.507
I'm fine.

917
01:22:08.012 --> 01:22:10.348
It's all right. Relax. Sit down.

918
01:22:15.186 --> 01:22:16.896
I know what you're all thinking.

919
01:22:18.397 --> 01:22:19.982
After what's gone on...

920
01:22:21.776 --> 01:22:24.862
I've been doing a little thinking myself,
believe it or not.

921
01:22:26.447 --> 01:22:29.158
And not too many of us are in love
with the tactics

922
01:22:29.242 --> 01:22:32.078
employed by our esteemed colleagues
in Langley, Virginia,

923
01:22:32.161 --> 01:22:33.788
but let me ask you all a question.

924
01:22:35.915 --> 01:22:38.668
They kill us and we kill them.

925
01:22:39.877 --> 01:22:43.172
I mean, does anybody here think
for a solitary second

926
01:22:43.506 --> 01:22:46.509
that if we stop killing them,
they're gonna stop killing us?

927
01:22:48.761 --> 01:22:52.098
It's a vicious cycle,
it doesn't matter who made it vicious.

928
01:22:53.266 --> 01:22:55.142
But they aren't gonna stop,

929
01:22:56.102 --> 01:22:57.436
so we can't.

930
01:22:58.437 --> 01:23:02.692
And that's why I'm gonna sit over
Afghanistan and Pakistan,

931
01:23:02.775 --> 01:23:05.653
Yemen, Somalia,
Sacramento-fucking-California,

932
01:23:06.445 --> 01:23:09.490
every day of what's left
of my sorry career

933
01:23:09.574 --> 01:23:12.285
if it saves one innocent American life.

934
01:23:12.660 --> 01:23:15.162
'Cause I got no idea in hell

935
01:23:17.123 --> 01:23:20.668
how to explain to some grieving parents
their son or daughter is dead

936
01:23:20.751 --> 01:23:23.337
because we thought
enough was enough.

937
01:23:23.796 --> 01:23:26.007
We declared victory and went home.

938
01:23:27.425 --> 01:23:29.427
It never ends,

939
01:23:30.219 --> 01:23:31.429
sir.

940
01:23:53.534 --> 01:23:55.286
<i>Prepare for a follow-up.</i>

941
01:24:16.349 --> 01:24:17.975
What would you like us to hit, sir?

942
01:24:25.858 --> 01:24:27.276
<i>Why aren't they responding?</i>

943
01:24:29.445 --> 01:24:34.575
Could it be perhaps that they think
you're gonna hit them again, Langley?

944
01:24:37.662 --> 01:24:40.414
What is it you'd like us to do, Langley?

945
01:24:40.998 --> 01:24:43.918
<i>If they can wait, so can we.</i>

946
01:24:44.502 --> 01:24:46.295
<i>What's our loiter time?</i>

947
01:24:48.005 --> 01:24:49.131
Eight hours.

948
01:24:50.049 --> 01:24:51.467
<i>Then we wait.</i>

949
01:25:14.365 --> 01:25:16.826
All this circling's
making me dizzy, Major.

950
01:25:18.494 --> 01:25:20.329
Can you at least go the other way?

951
01:25:25.251 --> 01:25:27.086
A vehicle approaching from the west.

952
01:25:27.586 --> 01:25:29.839
<i>We are identifying the target.</i>

953
01:25:33.634 --> 01:25:36.470
<i>Positive ID. Target qualifies.</i>

954
01:25:36.595 --> 01:25:38.097
<i>Permission to prosecute.</i>

955
01:25:42.435 --> 01:25:44.353
Should I bother pointing out
the non-combatants

956
01:25:44.437 --> 01:25:45.563
in the impact zone, sir?

957
01:25:46.856 --> 01:25:50.943
Or should I assume that
all collateral damage is proportionate?

958
01:25:51.569 --> 01:25:52.945
<i>Engage immediately.</i>

959
01:25:57.116 --> 01:25:58.117
<i>Laser.</i>

960
01:26:00.661 --> 01:26:01.871
<i>Laser.</i>

961
01:26:06.167 --> 01:26:07.251
Airman.

962
01:26:09.628 --> 01:26:10.838
Lasing.

963
01:26:12.047 --> 01:26:15.342
Master arm on, weapon's hot.

964
01:26:16.969 --> 01:26:18.971
Three, two...

965
01:26:23.267 --> 01:26:25.269
I've lost the link, sir.

966
01:26:25.352 --> 01:26:26.645
Yeah, I've lost the link.

967
01:26:27.813 --> 01:26:29.857
<i>Get it back. Reacquire.</i>

968
01:26:30.566 --> 01:26:32.318
Reaper in default setting.

969
01:26:32.943 --> 01:26:33.983
Automatic holding pattern.

970
01:26:34.320 --> 01:26:35.863
Attempting to reacquire now.

971
01:26:41.994 --> 01:26:43.788
Link re-established.

972
01:26:46.665 --> 01:26:49.293
- Shit.
- They've gotten away.

973
01:26:49.418 --> 01:26:51.462
<i>Locate the target. Find them.</i>

974
01:26:54.507 --> 01:26:56.258
<i>There. Strike the truck.</i>

975
01:26:56.342 --> 01:26:57.760
Yes, sir. Which one?

976
01:26:57.843 --> 01:26:59.094
<i>Hit the truck!</i>

977
01:26:59.595 --> 01:27:02.515
- Which <i>one, Langley?
- Jesus Christ!</i>

978
01:27:04.183 --> 01:27:05.935
Which truck, sir?

979
01:27:09.814 --> 01:27:11.190
Langley, which one?

980
01:27:11.899 --> 01:27:13.192
<i>Fuck!</i>

981
01:27:15.611 --> 01:27:16.987
Which one, sir?

982
01:27:18.447 --> 01:27:19.698
Which one?

983
01:27:24.161 --> 01:27:26.080
Captain Christie, take the controls.

984
01:27:33.003 --> 01:27:34.088
Major.

985
01:27:36.549 --> 01:27:37.591
Major.

986
01:27:50.563 --> 01:27:52.648
You deliberately dropped the link, Major.

987
01:27:52.898 --> 01:27:55.401
And last time I checked,
that's Article 92.

988
01:27:55.985 --> 01:27:57.778
Failure to comply with a lawful order.

989
01:27:59.446 --> 01:28:02.116
- And orders...
- Are orders.

990
01:28:09.415 --> 01:28:11.250
I gotta do something, Tommy.

991
01:28:13.460 --> 01:28:15.045
You tied my hands.

992
01:28:17.840 --> 01:28:20.759
If I don't do something,
the IT spooks will crawl up the ass

993
01:28:20.843 --> 01:28:23.762
of your console to work out
what we both know you did.

994
01:28:24.513 --> 01:28:26.682
And they'll come down on you
a fuck sight harder.

995
01:28:27.391 --> 01:28:28.392
I gotta do something.

996
01:28:31.270 --> 01:28:32.938
They're never gonna let it go.

997
01:28:39.528 --> 01:28:42.948
I guess this is a bad time to bring up
getting me back in a plane.

998
01:29:11.518 --> 01:29:12.937
Hey, Molly.

999
01:29:14.480 --> 01:29:15.564
Hi.

1000
01:29:16.565 --> 01:29:17.983
<i>You know that promotion?</i>

1001
01:29:20.235 --> 01:29:21.820
It got rescinded.

1002
01:29:23.155 --> 01:29:25.449
<i>I've been downgraded to surveillance.</i>

1003
01:29:25.741 --> 01:29:28.410
<i>- What'd you do?
- More like what I didn't do.</i>

1004
01:29:30.162 --> 01:29:32.164
I'm never gonna fly again.

1005
01:29:33.624 --> 01:29:35.000
I'm sorry.

1006
01:29:35.376 --> 01:29:36.835
<i>No, I'm sorry.</i>

1007
01:29:37.503 --> 01:29:40.339
<i>Look, this morning, how I left today...</i>

1008
01:29:40.422 --> 01:29:41.840
<i>- Tom my.
- Please, Molly.</i>

1009
01:29:41.924 --> 01:29:44.635
Tommy, I have something
I have to tell you.

1010
01:29:44.718 --> 01:29:47.596
<i>Please, Molly. Listen to me.</i>

1011
01:29:47.680 --> 01:29:49.431
<i>Give me a chance, all right?
I wanna make this up...</i>

1012
01:29:49.515 --> 01:29:52.351
I'm taking the kids
to my sister's in Reno.

1013
01:29:54.395 --> 01:29:56.063
When will you be back?

1014
01:29:58.107 --> 01:29:59.566
<i>I don't know.</i>

1015
01:30:02.277 --> 01:30:03.612
You're leaving me?

1016
01:30:07.950 --> 01:30:09.410
You left me first.

1017
01:30:10.995 --> 01:30:12.538
Molly, please.

1018
01:30:12.705 --> 01:30:15.207
I'm so sorry, Tommy. I've got to go.

1019
01:31:17.394 --> 01:31:19.605
Now I assume you know
we don't fly them

1020
01:31:19.688 --> 01:31:22.107
all the way there from here in Vegas,

1021
01:31:22.733 --> 01:31:23.817
but I guess I shouldn't assume anything.

1022
01:31:23.901 --> 01:31:25.944
I got food in my fridge
older than most of you.

1023
01:31:27.279 --> 01:31:30.324
Now, all take-offs and landings occur

1024
01:31:30.407 --> 01:31:32.409
in and around
whatever godforsaken place

1025
01:31:32.493 --> 01:31:33.827
we're at war with that day.

1026
01:31:47.800 --> 01:31:50.344
- You can't smoke here.
- Yeah, I know.

1027
01:31:58.811 --> 01:31:59.937
Sorry.

1028
01:32:02.481 --> 01:32:03.774
I heard your wife moved out.

1029
01:32:07.611 --> 01:32:10.072
Now they've stuck you
back on Kahili surveillance?

1030
01:32:10.614 --> 01:32:11.990
It's not your week.

1031
01:32:16.662 --> 01:32:18.163
I wanted to tell you

1032
01:32:19.373 --> 01:32:20.833
what happened with you,

1033
01:32:22.835 --> 01:32:24.253
I turned in my wings.

1034
01:32:27.131 --> 01:32:31.844
Yeah, can't make the battlefields
and blackjack thing work after all.

1035
01:32:39.685 --> 01:32:43.105
So I guess the order...

1036
01:32:44.690 --> 01:32:47.860
You know, the one prohibiting officers
and enlisted from fraternizing...

1037
01:32:49.611 --> 01:32:51.905
- Article 15.
- ...no longer applies.

1038
01:33:05.961 --> 01:33:06.962
If you change your mind.

1039
01:33:08.547 --> 01:33:11.633
The airman part's
a little misleading, but...

1040
01:33:14.553 --> 01:33:18.557
Make no mistake, I am first class.

1041
01:33:54.426 --> 01:33:55.719
Widen out.

1042
01:34:01.225 --> 01:34:03.518
Yeah, there's nothing going on here.

1043
01:34:04.436 --> 01:34:06.104
Why don't you two take a break.

1044
01:34:07.689 --> 01:34:11.109
I sure could use a break.
Thank you, Major.

1045
01:34:12.110 --> 01:34:13.403
Go on, Zim.

1046
01:34:13.612 --> 01:34:15.280
You can tell her all about
how close you were

1047
01:34:15.364 --> 01:34:18.283
to making that elite CT unit at Langley.

1048
01:34:56.154 --> 01:34:58.282
We're not gonna record anything today.

1049
01:35:02.828 --> 01:35:04.204
I got you.

1050
01:35:07.916 --> 01:35:10.168
All right, let's get a little closer.

1051
01:35:13.213 --> 01:35:14.923
Okay, there you are.

1052
01:35:15.841 --> 01:35:17.050
Going hot.

1053
01:35:21.805 --> 01:35:26.059
One Minnesota, two Minnesota...

1054
01:35:27.978 --> 01:35:29.813
You stay there. Okay, that's fine.

1055
01:35:30.480 --> 01:35:32.149
That's fine. Just stay put.

1056
01:35:32.941 --> 01:35:36.820
Three, two, one, rifle.

1057
01:35:37.529 --> 01:35:39.156
Time of flight, 10 seconds.

1058
01:35:42.075 --> 01:35:43.243
No, what are you doing?

1059
01:35:43.952 --> 01:35:46.788
No, no, no, go back. Stay back.

1060
01:35:46.872 --> 01:35:47.873
Get back...

1061
01:36:03.722 --> 01:36:05.015
Oh, my God.

1062
01:36:06.183 --> 01:36:09.186
Oh, please. Oh, please.

1063
01:36:11.021 --> 01:36:13.148
Oh, please, please,
please, please, please,

1064
01:36:13.231 --> 01:36:15.025
come on, come on, go...

1065
01:36:54.940 --> 01:36:57.317
Master arm off, weapon's safe.

1066
01:37:05.951 --> 01:37:07.244
Major Egan?

1067
01:37:19.714 --> 01:37:20.924
Egan.

1068
01:37:24.761 --> 01:37:25.929
Tommy.
